REMARK 400 THIS MODEL IS THAT OF THE C319Y MUTANT AT 2.0 ANGSTROMS.             
REMARK 400 THREE NONIDENTICAL CHAINS, GAMMA (A), BETA (B), AND ALPHA            
REMARK 400 (C) FORM ONE (ABC)-UNIT.  THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT CONTAINS ONE           
REMARK 400 (ABC)-UNIT.                                                          
REMARK 400 THE POSITION OF THE ACTIVE SITE FLAP IS SHIFTED BY UP TO 6           
REMARK 400 ANGSTROMS AS A RESULT OF THE MUTATION OF CYS319 - TYR.  THE          
REMARK 400 CATALYTICALLY IMPORTANT RESIDUE HIS 320 HAS SHIFTED BY 3.5           
REMARK 400 ANGSTROMS.                                                           
REMARK 400 THREE WATERS, 500, 501, AND 502 ARE LIGATED TO THE ACTIVE            
REMARK 400 SITE NICKEL IONS.  THEY MUST BE PARTIALLY OCCUPIED DUE TO            
REMARK 400 CLOSE OXYGEN-OXYGEN DISTANCES BETWEEN THEM.                          
